WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.872
Secure cameras before connecting them to a monitoring system.

00:00:04.872 --> 00:00:13.456
Change default credentials, use unique accounts, disable unused services, apply supported updates, and avoid direct internet exposure.

00:00:13.456 --> 00:00:18.328
Inventory model, firmware, owner, network address, and update status.

00:00:18.328 --> 00:00:25.057
Segment cameras, NVRs, inference servers, storage, and administrative systems according to required communication.

00:00:25.057 --> 00:00:29.929
Firewalls should permit only necessary streams and management paths.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:36.657
Remote access should use a controlled entry point with strong authentication and logging.

00:00:36.657 --> 00:00:46.169
Protect stored video, thumbnails, metadata, model prompts, and review notes with encryption where appropriate, access control, and retention policy.

00:00:46.169 --> 00:00:56.145
Local AI servers require operating-system and driver patching, least privilege, secure administration, and protection of API keys or alert credentials.

00:00:56.145 --> 00:01:03.801
Back up configuration, camera maps, rules, model versions, and review metadata according to recovery needs.

00:01:03.801 --> 00:01:08.673
Test restoration without retaining more video than policy permits.

00:01:08.673 --> 00:01:14.474
Keep a known-good way to rebuild or replace the inference host.

00:01:14.474 --> 00:01:25.842
Monitor the complete pipeline: camera reachability, stream decode, frame rate, inference latency, accelerator health, storage capacity, event creation, dashboard access, and alert delivery.

00:01:25.842 --> 00:01:33.962
A green server status is not enough if the camera is frozen or notifications are failing.

00:01:33.962 --> 00:01:36.050
Define fail-safe expectations.

00:01:36.050 --> 00:01:45.562
When the model, network, or camera is unavailable, the system should report degraded coverage rather than imply normal awareness.

00:01:45.562 --> 00:01:54.146
Practice incident response, preserve relevant logs, and restore trustworthy operation without broadening data access during the emergency.
